UPDATE public.spots SET access = '{"shore": true, "notes": "Much of the prime water is allocated through New Brunswick''s Crown Reserve system — a limited-entry fishery assigning stretches on a rod-per-day basis by draw, with 20 regular stretches across the Miramichi and Restigouche systems. Miramichi Crown Reserve licences run 48 hours (2pm on day one to 2pm on day three) and do not guarantee exclusive use of the stretch; they are non-refundable. Named Miramichi stretches include Adams Pool, Charlies Rock, Crawford, Depot, Elbow, Groundhog Landing, Narrows, Squirrel Falls, Stoney Brook and Sullivan, each with published directions and pool maps. Regular Crown Reserve runs 10 June to 15 September. Fly fishing only, restricted to a barbless artificial fly; September is live release only for all species. Water outside the Crown Reserve system is a mix of private beats and public stretches — check locally before fishing.", "sourceUrl": "https://www2.gnb.ca/content/gnb/en/departments/erd/fish-and-wildlife/content/go-fishing/content/CrownReserveStretches/Miramichi.html"}'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'miramichi-atlantic-salmon';
